Teodoro, on Desmond's point about flagged folders, that flag is the whole m=
echanism and it needs to be built before the new schedule takes effect, not=
 after.<br />
<br />
When a hold is placed on a project, nothing in that project folder may be t=
iered, migrated, overwritten or deleted, regardless of what the retention s=
chedule says about its age. The hold has to sit at the project folder level=
, it has to be visible to anyone who opens the folder, and it has to surviv=
e a tier change. A retention schedule that automation can apply to a folder=
 under hold is worse than no schedule at all.<br />
<br />
I would also like the hold list reviewed quarterly by contracts rather than=
 annually, because holds get placed and then forgotten and material stays f=
rozen for years after a matter closes.